% Regressions from the Go implementation review, 2026-09-29.
% Expected behavior is shared by all hosts. Concurrency is tested in Go.

### name: record.shape.nul-boundaries
--- note
Distinct key tuples with equal NUL-joined bytes must retain distinct shapes (§3). Equal field counts avoid relying on a host crash to detect the collision.
--- source
A = RECORD("a\u{0}b", 11, "c", 12); RECORD("a", 21, "b\u{0}c", 22)["a"]
--- expect
num 21
===

### name: record.shape.nul-field-count
--- note
A single key containing NUL must not reuse the shape of two separate keys.
--- source
A = RECORD("d", 1, "e", 2); RECORD("d\u{0}e", 3)["d\u{0}e"]
--- expect
num 3
===

### name: integer.width.power
--- note
Size arguments must be checked or clamped before conversion to a machine integer (§6.4 and the individual built-in contract).
--- source
POWER(2,18446744073709551616)
--- expect
error E_RANGE
===

